--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5 + [temp.alias]/2.  A MEMBER alias template
whose body expands two parallel packs (its own pack + the enclosing class's
pack) -- the shape of libstdc++'s std::tuple _TupleConstraints
(__constructible/__convertible = __and_<is_X<_Types, _UTypes>...>).  The
two-parallel-pack EXPANSION itself is now fixed (the alias's own-pack expansion
is deferred out of class instantiation so `sums<int,double,char>` correctly
resolves to `sum_t<1,1,1>`, commit "defer a member alias template's own-pack
expansion during class instantiation").  The non-type-pack `sizeof...` count bug
that also obscured this is fixed too (commit "count a non-type parameter pack in
sizeof...(P) correctly"; see cpp11_nontype_value_pack_fn_template, now CORE).
This test nonetheless remains a KNOWNBUG because of a further SEPARATE residual:
a recursive non-type-pack trait value (`sum_t<...>::v`, where `sum_t` recurses
over its own pack) instantiated with a pack FORWARDED from an enclosing function
template (`sums<Us...>::v` in `chk`) does not fold, so `chk()` is left
unconstrained rather than the constant 3.  A minimal witness is
`sum_t<sizeof(Us)...>::v` accessed inside such a `chk`.  Flip to CORE once that
residual is fixed.
